      "writtenOn": "2021-09-23T02:16:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if we should put a lower limit on this number than 2^16. A fake FMAP structure could force the GSC to read up to (42 * 2^16) ~\u003d 2-3MB from flash here, and that is per fake FMAP (of which there could potentially be many in the RW section at higher alignments than the real FMAP). Realistically, something like 64 entries per FMAP should be more than we\u0027ll likely ever need and should limit this to a manageable level.",
      "revId": "e272a15aab408f1d370ed0383f3db203106dabe0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
